WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.789
Despite originally refusing to remove controversial
footage included in its horror hit Bird Box,

00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:07.000
Netflix has now changed its mind.

00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:11.120
The film stars Sandra Bullock as a single
mother living in a post-apocalyptic world

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.840
where monsters convince humans to commit suicide
if they catch sight of them.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.380
The Canadian Press confirms that the streamer
will remove from Bird Box footage of the real-life

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.880
Lac-Mégantic rail disaster that took place
in 2013.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.960
An unnamed spokesperson for the streaming
giant released an email statement to the outlet

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.600
that reads:

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.140
"Netflix and the filmmakers of Bird Box have
decided to replace the clip.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.620
We're sorry for any pain caused to the Lac-Mégantic
community."

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.040
For those unaware, the initial cut of Bird
Box includes footage from a train crash that

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.200
happened on July 6, 2013 in Lac-Mégantic,
Quebec, Canada.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.440
That day, a freight train loaded with crude
oil derailed from the tracks and crashed.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.340
Several of the train's cars exploded and then
caught fire.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.380
The accident left 47 people dead, a large
portion of Lac-Mégantic's downtown buildings

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.280
completely destroyed, and most of the city's
downtown area ruined and in need of rebuilding.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.440
Clips of the train tragedy appear within the
first few minutes of Bird Box, during the

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.320
scene in which Malorie and her sister Jessica
are watching the news on television.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.280
They see massive explosions and total devastation
wracking a town - footage meant in the film

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.219
to indicate that the world is experiencing
a mass epidemic of unexplained violence.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.140
"The eyewitness reports tell of people experiencing
psychotic behavior."

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.200
Netflix reportedly obtained the clips from
stock footage company Pond5, where individuals

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.880
can purchase images and clips, including those
from newscasts that depict sensitive events.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.480
Another of the streamer's projects, the sci-fi
television show Travelers, also implemented

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:40.429
Lac-Mégantic disaster footage, which Travelers'
production company Peacock Alley Entertainment

00:01:40.429 --> 00:01:44.310
stated wasn't intended to "dishonor the tragic
events of 2013."

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:49.340
A spokesperson from Pond5 also issued an apology
for the use of the footage in Travelers:

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.540
"We deeply regret that this happened and sincerely
apologize to anyone who was offended, especially

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:58.419
the victims and their families … We are
contacting all customers who have purchased

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.420
any related clips to ensure they are aware
of the sensitive nature of this footage.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.940
Additionally, we're proactively re-auditing
content of this nature, while continuing to

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.679
improve our guidance for usage."

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:12.731
When Netflix was made aware of the situation
as it relates to Bird Box, however, the streamer

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.720
refused to remove the footage at first.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.480
A spokesperson indicated that Netflix would
keep the clip in the movie, and would be,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.740
quote, "looking at ways to do things differently
moving forward."

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.540
Many were outraged at Netflix's original decision,
none more than Lac-Mégantic Mayor Julie Morin

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.720
and Quebec Culture Minister Nathalie Roy.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.940
Morin wrote that the use of the footage and
subsequent refusal to take it out of Bird

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.700
Box after knowing all the facts showed a complete
lack of respect for the people of Lac-Mégantic

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.990
and those affected by the 2013 disaster.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:41.980
She said:

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.000
"It's hard enough for our citizens to see
these images when they are used normally and

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.420
respectfully on the news.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.800
Just imagine, to have them used as fiction,
as if they were invented."

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.230
Roy singled out Netflix CEO Reed Hastings
for criticism, writing that Netflix was exhibiting

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:00.450
a, quote, "lack of compassion, empathy, and
solidarity" in its decision.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.450
She also stated that the Quebec government
found it unbelievable that Netflix wouldn't

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.370
remove the clips from Bird Box or think that
it was okay to implement them in the first

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:08.860
place.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.620
"I think it's a huge mistake.”

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.019
Now that Netflix has reversed its choice - having
already updated the film as of the making

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:19.650
of this video - Morin is satisfied and willing
to look past the streamer's initial refusal.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.140
She said:

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.980
"Yes, there was a delay, but I think in the
end, what's more important for me, is that

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:27.510
we have a solution to this situation we felt
was important to settle."

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.819
Morin further noted that the entertainment
industry needs to "reflect on this" and other

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:36.230
situations like this to hopefully create a
new standard for the use of stock footage

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.980
in films and television series.

